 "_units": "lungePx / hopPx / anims.*.lunge are PMD-scale pixels (converted from GIF pixels by the pixelize scale)",
 "_comment": "gen9 curation. Most gen9 GIFs (19/20 frames) are two idle halves with baked-in move effects: a mouth beam (frames 3-8 / 4-9) and a slash or burst (12-16 / 13-17). Idle is trimmed to the effect-free opening frames; the effect frames drive Shoot / SpAttack / Strike. The long legendary GIFs (wo-chien, chien-pao, gouging-fire) are several identical breathing loops plus one action sequence; Idle is one loop and the action sequence drives the moves. Pixel tuning: pixelHeight is matched to comparable gen9 PMD sheets (e.g. Great Tusk 34, Walking Wake 40, Koraidon 44); textured GIFs use fewer colours, larger speckSize and a higher innerLines threshold so the source texture strokes do not turn into black noise.",
